# ==============================================================================
# Destination Domain Transport Map (/etc/postfix/transport)
# Copy this file to config/transport (or set TRANSPORT_MAPS in .env) to forward
# specific destination domains to specific MX / SMTP relay servers.
# ==============================================================================
#
# Syntax:
#   destination-domain      transport:[nexthop]:port
#
# Note: Putting brackets [ ] around the nexthop hostname/IP disables MX lookups
# and connects directly to that host/IP. Omit brackets to perform MX lookup.
#
# Examples:
#
# 1. Forward all mail for partner.com directly to a specific SMTP server on port 25:
# partner.com               smtp:[203.0.113.55]:25
#
# 2. Forward internal corporate domain to internal Exchange/Zimbra relay on port 2525:
# internal.company.com      smtp:[10.20.30.10]:2525
#
# 3. Force a specific destination domain to use Outbound VIP 1 AND a specific MX server:
# vip-partner.org           smtp_vip1:[mx.vip-partner.org]:25
#
# 4. Force a specific destination domain (e.g. outlook.com) to use Outbound VIP 3:
# outlook.com               smtp_vip3:
